--cpp20
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Class-template partial specialization selected via a conditional-operator
SFINAE check (`void_t<decltype(false ? declval<A>() : declval<B>())>`) when the
specialization is a MEMBER of a class template.  N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match]/2,
[temp.deduct]/8, [expr.cond]/4, [class.default.ctor]/3.  The minimal essence of
libstdc++'s C++20 `__common_ref_impl<_Xp&, _Yp&, void_t<__condres_cvref<_Xp,_Yp>>>`
family.

For `cref<int, int*>` the conditional has no common type, so the specialization
is rejected and the primary is used (`tag == 1`).  Previously the primary
fallback was still incomplete at the enclosing class's constructor-synthesis
time, so its default member initializer was dropped from the constructor and the
member read uninitialised, while a cleanly-matched member (`cref<int, int>`) was
already complete -- an inconsistency.  Fixed by elaborating a member's
class-template-instance type before deciding whether its default construction is
non-trivial ([class.default.ctor]/3 + [temp.inst]/2).
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
